# Components

## Framework semantics

Components provide reusable controller-layer helpers and callback integration (`startup`, `beforeRender`, etc.). They are not middleware substitutes and must not own persistence or domain invariants.

## Required behavior

- Prefer Components for shared controller collaboration tightly coupled to controller callbacks.
- Prefer Middleware for PSR request/response pipeline work that should run regardless of controller.
- Keep Components HTTP/orchestration helpers only — Tables own persistence.
- Avoid god Components that accumulate unrelated Flash/Auth/billing/API concerns.

## Anti-patterns

- god-component
- Using Components as a global request pipeline (use middleware)
- Persistence concern in component

## Review checklist

- [ ] Reuse is controller-scoped, not pipeline-global
- [ ] No Table/save/query ownership hidden in the Component
- [ ] Auth identity loading still follows project middleware norms when that is the convention
